Well, the way I was originally thinkng of it, there would be a particular
item, a potion of enchantment, that you would need to find in order to
enchant anything, and in order to keep the game from getting unbalanced,
this would have to be a hell of a rare item... about as rare as wands of
death, although maybe not as rare as wands of wishing... In fact, here's
how to make it very balanced: Each time when you start the game and its
randomly assigning names (Foobie Bletch) to scrolls, it randomly assigns
a list of ingredients to each possible makable item. So that in order
to make a weapon into a weapon of paralysis, you would need:
a potion of enchantment (very arare), a potion of paralysis, one
randomly selected gem, and one randomly selected food item. The only way
to find out the ingredients would be to pay large sums of money to delphi,
or to pray for guidance, or to complete some other as-yet-undefined
side quest. So in order to make one item you would have to 
(a) figure out the recipe and
(b) find a potion of enchantment
and
(c) find the other ingredients (which might not be easy if its a rare
gem)
